  "final_message": "Done. The todo app is complete and verified:\n\n**Backend** (`backend/app.py`) \u2014 Flask + SQLite (`./data/todos.db`, stdlib `sqlite3`, no new deps):\n- `POST /api/auth/register` (201), `POST /api/auth/login` (200 + `{\"token\"}`), Bearer-token auth (401 otherwise)\n- Todos CRUD: `GET/POST /api/todos`, `GET/PATCH/DELETE /api/todos/{id}` (404 for other users' todos), `completed_at` set on completion / cleared on reopen\n- Paged list `{\"items\",\"total\",\"page\",\"page_size\",\"remaining\"}` with `completed`/`priority` filters, sorted open-first \u2192 due date (nulls last) \u2192 newest first; field-level validation messages (`{\"error\", \"fields\"}`)\n- Serves `frontend/dist` and `GET /api/health`\n\n**Frontend** (`frontend/`) \u2014 React + TS + Vite + Tailwind v4 (`@tailwindcss/vite`, single `src/index.css` entry): register/sign-in forms, username + sign out, add form and inline editing with API validation messages, priority badges, overdue highlighting, instant checkbox saving, open-todo counter, All/Open/Completed tabs, priority filter, Load more, confirm-before-delete.\n\n**Fix**: `backend/requirements.txt` now carries the pinned hashes (mirroring `requirements.lock`) \u2014 pip's hash-checking mode (triggered by the hashed constraints file) rejects unhashed direct requirements, so the Docker `pip install -r \u2026 -c \u2026` step failed on the scaffold as-is; it works now in every mode.\n\nVerified with 56 end-to-end API checks (auth, validation, sorting, paging, isolation, `completed_at` lifecycle) plus a Docker-CMD-equivalent smoke test and restart persistence; `npm ci && npm run build` succeeds from the lockfile.",
  "final_message_truncated": false,
